# Docker build context for `docker build -f engines/python/Dockerfile .` (context = repository root).
# Deny by default: only the Python engine's sources enter the context, so nothing else in the tree
# (private or dev material, other engines, tests, caches, the git history) can reach the daemon or an
# image, including paths added later. Order matters: the last matching rule wins.
*
!engines
engines/*
!engines/python
**/tests
**/dist
**/build
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
